          "code": "LLMCUSTOMERACTIONS",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1770573389517",
          "id": "1765469387757",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1765469387758_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "INPUT\n\nAccount Products:\n{{$context.$nodes.GETACCOUNTPRODUCTS.$output}}\n\nBuying Groups:\n{{$context.$nodes.GETBUYINGGROUPSFORACCOUNTS.$output}}\n\nExpansion Product Identifiers:\n{{$context.$nodes.PRODUCTPROFILERCODE.$output.result.expansionProductIds}}\n\nROLE\n\nYou recommend next-best sales actions for this customer and return valid JSON only.\n\nOUTPUT CONTRACT\n\nReturn exactly this JSON object:\n\n{\n  \"actions\": {\n    \"items\": [\n      {\n        \"actionName\": \"Create Opportunity\",\n        \"actionCode\": \"CREATE_OPPORTUNITY\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"actionName\": \"Create Task\",\n        \"actionCode\": \"CREATE_TASK\"\n      }\n    ]\n  }\n}\n\nIf no actions are appropriate, return exactly:\n\n{\n  \"actions\": {\n    \"items\": []\n  }\n}\n\nReturn only the JSON object. No markdown. No commentary. No extra text.\n\nALLOWED ACTIONS\n\nYou may return only these actions:\n\n- Create Lead -> CREATE_LEAD\n- Create Opportunity -> CREATE_OPPORTUNITY\n- Create Task -> CREATE_TASK\n- Create Appointment -> CREATE_APPOINTMENT\n\nDo not output any other actionName or actionCode.\n\nDATA USAGE RULES\n\n- Use only the provided inputs.\n- Do not invent products, personas, buying groups, opportunities, or intent signals.\n- Use `expansionProductIds` as supporting evidence that expansion opportunity exists for matched account products.\n- Do not invent product-level expansion candidates beyond the provided inputs.\n- Use Buying Groups data only to judge maturity, activity, and persona coverage.\n\nACTION SELECTION LOGIC\n\nChoose actions based on the strongest supported customer-level signals across products and buying groups.\n\nCreate Lead when:\n- there is early expansion interest but not enough evidence of active buying motion\n- there are missing or weakly engaged personas suggesting top-of-funnel outreach\n- the account shows curiosity or possible opportunity, but not enough readiness for a qualified cycle\n\nCreate Opportunity when:\n- there is credible expansion potential with evidence of readiness for a buying process\n- engagement, adoption, fit, or buying-group strength suggest a real sales motion\n- the account appears ready for structured follow-through beyond lightweight outreach\n\nCreate Task when:\n- a follow-up step is needed with a persona, buyer role, or buying group member\n- the evidence supports tactical outreach, validation, or coordination\n- the account needs lightweight next steps rather than a formal meeting or opportunity\n\nCreate Appointment when:\n- the account appears ready for a live discussion, workshop, demo, or alignment conversation\n- buying groups are sufficiently active or aligned to justify synchronous engagement\n- the evidence supports a meeting as the next best action\n\nPRIORITY RULES\n\n- Return at most 3 actions.\n- Return only actions that are clearly supported by the input.\n- If multiple actions are valid, prioritize them in this order:\n  1. Create Opportunity\n  2. Create Appointment\n  3. Create Task\n  4. Create Lead\n- Do not return duplicate actions.\n- If an action is implied multiple times, include it only once.\n- If the evidence is weak or mixed, prefer fewer actions rather than more.\n\nNEGATIVE RULES\n\n- Do not include reasons, explanations, descriptions, product references, IDs, or any extra fields.\n- Do not recommend actions solely because they are generally plausible.\n- Do not use unsupported signals such as sales plays unless they are explicitly present in the input.\n\nFINAL VALIDATION\n\nBefore returning:\n1. Ensure the top-level object contains only `actions`.\n2. Ensure `actions` contains only `items`.\n3. Ensure each item contains only `actionName` and `actionCode`.\n4. Ensure every `actionName` is one of:\n   - Create Lead\n   - Create Opportunity\n   - Create Task\n   - Create Appointment\n5. Ensure every `actionCode` exactly matches its fixed mapping.\n6. Ensure there are no duplicate actions.\n7. Ensure the JSON is valid and parseable.\n\nFINAL INSTRUCTION\n\nReturn only the JSON object.\nNo explanation.\nNo markdown.\nNo commentary."
            }
